# The rules that actually run live at the git repository root.
#
#   ../../.easignore      (D:/Jubair Islam Daief/Ranna Bari/.easignore)
#
# EAS CLI builds its upload archive starting from the root of the git
# repository, not from the project, and it reads `.easignore` from that same
# root. A copy here is never opened in the normal `eas build` path — this file
# once held the real rules, and the build uploaded 594 MB anyway because
# nothing read them. Verified since with `eas build:inspect --stage archive`:
# 594 MB before, 13 MB after moving them up.
#
# The entries below are kept only for the one case where this location IS
# read: running with `EAS_NO_VCS=1`, which archives from the project root
# instead. They are a subset of the root file — if you change one, change both.

node_modules/

.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo
expo-env.d.ts

# Generated by prebuild on the builder itself.
/ios
/android
.kotlin/

# Scratch directories from headless-browser verification runs.
.smoke/
.exportcheck/
.expo-export-check/
.claude/

# Secrets never belong in a build archive. Build-time configuration goes in
# eas.json under the profile's `env`, which is where EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is.
.env
.env.*
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
